# The first variant. repetition: row 1 was darker than the rest (ΔL* 4.1): seven dark marks at
# 0,1 3,1 12,1 13,1 19,1 22,1 23,1 make a dashed line across the floor when tiled; row 17 was
# the lightest. The dash at 12,1-13,1 and the mark at 22,1 move down into row 17, where a light
# mark makes room.
px 12,1 13,1 22,1 c=moss2
px 10,17 c=moss2
px 13,17 14,17 c=moss1
# seam was 0.97, close to the limit: row 0's light marks at 17,0 19,0 stood against row 23.
px 17,0 19,0 c=moss2
# A doubled corner in the dash at 2,4-2,5 (jaggies, within the tile's allowance): it steps
# diagonally now.
px 2,5 c=moss2
# The same V tufts as the base tile, made unalike.
px 11,5 10,8 c=moss2
px 7,17 8,20 c=moss2
